<header class="page-hero">
  <h1>See ADS-B traffic in your navigation app</h1>
  <p class="page-hero-subtitle">skyBlip Bravo detects Mode S and ADS-B transponders. Aircraft with ADS-B transmit their position by radio. Bravo sends that traffic over Bluetooth to a compatible navigation app such as SDVFR or SkyDemon. The MeshTracker X1 has no screen. In flight the device sounds and vibrates if traffic triggers an alert.</p>
  <figure class="hero-figure">
    <%= pages_image_tag "seeed-x1.avif", alt: "The Seeed SenseCAP MeshTracker X1, a black card-sized device with a green button." %>
    <figcaption class="pair-caption">Photo: Seeed Studio.</figcaption>
  </figure>
</header>

<section id="status" class="band band--tint">
  <h2 class="section-title">See aircraft you already fly alongside</h2>
  <p>Bravo sees newer aircraft fitted with ADS-B and older aircraft upgraded with a glass cockpit connected to an ADS-B transmitter or with a new ADS-B transponder. Near an airfield or airport, you also see airliners, business jets and helicopters that transmit ADS-B.</p>
  <p>Bravo also detects Mode S transponders without ADS-B. They give no position. We&rsquo;re collecting data from those detections to work out how best to report them on Go and in navigation apps. Bravo receives these signals directly on board at 1090 MHz, without a ground station. It doesn&rsquo;t receive ADS-L, the European standard for sharing position by radio, or FLARM, a position-sharing system widely used in gliding. It doesn&rsquo;t transmit your position.</p>
  <p>Bravo is an uncertified aid to visual lookout.</p>
</section>

<section id="with-go" class="band">
  <h2 class="section-title">Add this traffic to Go&rsquo;s radar</h2>
  <p>Already have a Go? Pair it with Bravo to make a Tango. Go shows ADS-B alongside ADS-L and FLARM on its radar. It keeps transmitting your position in ADS-L.</p>
</section>

<section id="buy" class="band band--tint">
  <h2 class="section-title">Looking for a MeshTracker X1?</h2>
  <p>Buy the hardware, then install the skyBlip Bravo software. The software that comes with the X1 doesn&rsquo;t receive ADS-B.</p>
